% Section 1 of the British Nationality Act 1981, after the logic program of
% Sergot, Sadri, Kowalski, Kriwaczek, Hammond and Cory (1986). Anna, born in
% the UK after commencement to a settled father, is a British citizen, and so
% is her son Ben, through her. Hugo was born before commencement, Dara before
% her father settled, and Jo abroad; none of them is a citizen by section 1.
% The foundling Eve is a citizen; for Finn the contrary is shown.
% Shows templates, alternatives grouped by indentation, "it is not the case
% that", date comparisons, a scenario and its expected answers.

the templates are:
    *a person* is a British citizen,
    *a person* is a qualifying parent of *a person*,
    *a person* is a parent of *a person*,
    *a person* is born in *a place* on *a date*,
    *a person* is found as a new-born infant in *a place* on *a date*,
    *a person* is settled in the UK since *a date*,
    *a date* is after commencement,
    the contrary is shown for *a person*.

the knowledge base british nationality act includes:

% Section 1(1): born in the UK after commencement to a parent who was then a
% British citizen or settled in the UK.
a person is a British citizen
    if the person is born in the UK on a date
    and the date is after commencement
    and an other person is a qualifying parent of the person.

% Section 1(2): found abandoned in the UK as a new-born infant after
% commencement, unless the contrary is shown.
a person is a British citizen
    if the person is found as a new-born infant in the UK on a date
    and the date is after commencement
    and it is not the case that
        the contrary is shown for the person.

% The deeper lines bind tighter: a parent qualifies as a citizen, or as
% settled on or before the birth.
a person is a qualifying parent of an other person
    if the person is a parent of the other person
    and the person is a British citizen
        or the other person is born in a place on a date
            and the person is settled in the UK since a second date
            and the second date is before or equal to the date.

% The Act commenced on 1 January 1983.
a date is after commencement
    if the date is after or equal to 1983-01-01.

% Gwen is a citizen under earlier law, which this program does not model.
scenario families is:
    Farid is a parent of Anna.
    Farid is settled in the UK since 1975-03-01.
    Anna is born in the UK on 1990-05-12.
    Anna is a parent of Ben.
    Ben is born in the UK on 2015-08-20.
    Anna is a parent of Jo.
    Jo is born in France on 2017-02-03.
    Gwen is a British citizen.
    Gwen is a parent of Hugo.
    Hugo is born in the UK on 1980-01-01.
    Ivan is a parent of Dara.
    Ivan is settled in the UK since 2005-01-01.
    Dara is born in the UK on 2001-03-04.
    Eve is found as a new-born infant in the UK on 2020-06-01.
    Finn is found as a new-born infant in the UK on 2018-01-01.
    the contrary is shown for Finn.
    citizens expects answers ["Anna is a British citizen", "Ben is a British citizen",
        "Eve is a British citizen", "Gwen is a British citizen"].
    parents expects answers ["Farid is a qualifying parent of Anna", "Anna is a qualifying parent of Ben",
        "Anna is a qualifying parent of Jo", "Gwen is a qualifying parent of Hugo"].

query citizens is:
    which person is a British citizen.

query parents is:
    which person is a qualifying parent of which other person.
